{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.C1DeterminantRelation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1DeterminantRelation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.C1ZeroSideExponents"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.both_ends_consistent_with_detA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.both_ends_consistent_with_detA","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1DeterminantRelation.lean#L173-L180","doc":"**Both ends consistent with the same determinant.**  Recorded as one\nstatement because the point is that a *single* object — `a₀/a₂` — reproduces two\nindependently computed exponent pairs.  Neither end was fitted to the other. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.irregular_end_consistent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.irregular_end_consistent","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1DeterminantRelation.lean#L165-L171","doc":"**The `∞`-end check.**  After factoring out the simple zero, `det A`'s\nleading coefficient at `∞` is `−(q−1)/q²`; scaled by `q²` that is `−(q−1)`,\nexactly `edge_roots_mul`.  The Newton polygon at `∞` and `a₀/a₂` agree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.detA_at_infty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.detA_at_infty","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1DeterminantRelation.lean#L157-L163","doc":"`det A` in the coordinate `u = 1/x` at `∞`: a simple zero,\n`det A = −(q−1)·u/(q² − u)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.edge_roots_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.edge_roots_mul","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1DeterminantRelation.lean#L149-L155","doc":"**The `∞`-end product.**  The two edge roots multiply to `−(q−1)/q²`, i.e.\n`q²·(t·s) = −(q−1)`.  Note this is *strictly more* than the edge equation, which\nonly constrains each root's square. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.edge_roots_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.edge_roots_neg","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1DeterminantRelation.lean#L136-L147","doc":"Two distinct roots of the Newton-edge equation `q²t² = q − 1` are negatives\nof each other — the deck sign, arrived at here from the edge equation rather than\nfrom the ramified cover. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.fuchsian_end_consistent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.fuchsian_end_consistent","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1DeterminantRelation.lean#L125-L132","doc":"**The `0`-end check.**  The product of the two local exponents equals\n`det A(0)`.  Vieta's constant term and `a₀/a₂` at `x = 0` were computed from\ndifferent data and agree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.detA_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.detA_zero","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1DeterminantRelation.lean#L120-L123","doc":"`det A` at the Fuchsian point: `det A(0) = q − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.indicial_roots_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.indicial_roots_mul","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1DeterminantRelation.lean#L114-L118","doc":"**Vieta, product** — likewise derived from `C1ZeroSide.vieta`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.indicial_roots_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.indicial_roots_add","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1DeterminantRelation.lean#L105-L112","doc":"**Vieta, sum** — derived from the pre-existing `C1ZeroSide.vieta` rather\nthan reproved.  An earlier version of this file carried its own proof; that\nduplicated `qou-wgnx` work and is retired. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.detA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.detA","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1DeterminantRelation.lean#L100-L101","doc":"`det A` of C1's companion system: `a₀/a₂ = −(q−1)/(q²x − 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.indicialAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.indicialAt","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1DeterminantRelation.lean#L94-L98","doc":"The indicial polynomial at `0`.  **Not redefined here** — this is\n`QOU.QBeta.C1ZeroSide.zeroSideIndicial`, which predates this file (bean\n`qou-wgnx`).  An earlier version of this file defined its own copy under the name\n`indicialAt`; that was duplication and is retired. ","signatureChunk":0}]}